  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). No intransitive pair.\n\nWRITING:\nAlso written {煎|い}る. Both kanji are used, though {炒|い}る is more common for dry-roasting in a pan.\n\nDISTINCTION FROM {炒|いた}める:\n{炒|い}る refers to dry roasting without oil (seeds, beans, tea leaves), while {炒|いた}める means to stir-fry with oil (vegetables, meat). This distinction is important in cooking contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ごまを{炒|い}る: to roast sesame seeds\n- {豆|まめ}を{炒|い}る: to roast beans\n- コーヒー{豆|まめ}を{炒|い}る: to roast coffee beans",
